# artifacts/api-server — environment contract.
#
# BUG-228: this file listed 4 variables while the server read 10. Every
# variable the server reads is now here, with what it does and what happens
# when it is absent. NEVER put a real secret in this file.
#
# 🔴 = secret, belongs in Secret Manager on a deployed instance.
# ⚪ = plain config, safe as a deploy variable.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 🔴 Postgres connection string (Neon).
# ⚠️ ABSENT OR WRONG IS THE DANGEROUS ONE AND IT DOES NOT CRASH: the process
#    boots, logs `prisma_connect_failed`, and /api/healthz still answers 200
#    while every real request 503s. That is BUG-221, and it is why /api/readyz
#    exists — readiness runs SELECT 1 and is the check a deploy should gate on.
DATABASE_URL=""

# 🔴 JWT signing secret for session, password-reset and email-change tokens.
# Absent: the process THROWS at import of lib/auth.ts. Loud, immediate, correct.
JWT_SECRET=""

# ⚪ TCP port to listen on. Absent: throws at boot with a named error.
# Cloud Run injects this automatically (8080); set it locally.
PORT="3000"

# ── Optional, but wrong-by-default if unset ─────────────────────────────

# ⚪ Set to "production" on any deployed instance.
# ⚠️ Absent is SILENT AND WRONG: pino loads the pino-pretty transport and emits
#    ANSI-coloured text instead of JSON, so structured fields stop being
#    queryable in a log sink. It also leaves the dev-only global Prisma guard on.
NODE_ENV="development"

# ⚪ pino level. Absent: "info".
LOG_LEVEL="info"

# ⚪ How many proxy hops in front of this app to trust when deriving the client
# address for rate limiting. Absent: 0 — trust nothing, measured byte-identical
# to leaving Express's `trust proxy` unset.
#
# 🔴 THE VALUE IS REASONED, NOT MEASURED. DO NOT SET IT BEFORE THE TWO-NETWORK
#    CURL AGAINST A REAL DEPLOYMENT. BUG-223's own measurement: deploy any
#    revision with one line logging `remoteAddress` and `x-forwarded-for`, then
#    curl from two different networks. Cloud Run is expected to want 1 (one hop,
#    Google's front end) — expected, not confirmed.
# ⚠️ MUST NAME THE HOP COUNT, NEVER `true`. `true` trusts the whole chain and
#    hands a spoofer back the identity-rotation hole the limiter closes. The
#    parser refuses "true" and every non-integer, falling back to 0.
TRUST_PROXY_HOPS="0"

# ── AI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 🔴 Anthropic key. Absent: runAICall returns a typed { reason: "no_api_key" }
# failure — every AI feature degrades, the server stays up and serves.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# 🔴 USDA FoodData Central (data.gov) key for ingredient nutrition enrichment.
# Optional: when unset, USDA enrichment no-ops silently and macros fall back
# to the AI dish-level estimator (today's behavior).
USDA_INGREDIENTS_API_KEY=""

# ⚪ Store-compose shortlist size. Absent: 40. Parsed and clamped; garbage
# falls back to the default rather than throwing.
KIWI_STORE_SHORTLIST_SIZE="40"

# ⚪ Fraction [0,1] of the shelf reserved for cuisine matches. Absent: 0.7.
# Clamped to [0,1]; garbage falls back to the default.
KIWI_STORE_CUISINE_QUOTA_FRACTION="0.7"

# ── Email (BUG-224) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 🔴 Resend API key. Absent: lib/email/sendEmail.ts returns a typed
# { reason: "no_api_key" } no-op, and password-reset and email-change behave
# exactly as they did before the seam existed — token minted, nothing sent,
# route returns its normal anti-enumeration success.
# ⚠️ KEY PRESENCE IS THE ONLY GATE. There is deliberately no NODE_ENV check,
#    because a test or a Neon-branch smoke run may legitimately run with
#    NODE_ENV=production; not having a key is what makes them unable to send.
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# ⚪ Envelope sender, e.g. "Kiwi <noreply@send.example.com>".
# ⚠️ REQUIRED WHENEVER RESEND_API_KEY IS SET — the process throws at boot if a
#    key is present and this is not, rather than sending mail that bounces.
# Must be on a Resend-verified domain or every send is rejected.
EMAIL_FROM=""

# ⚪ Base https URL the server builds emailed links from, no trailing slash,
# e.g. "https://app.example.com". Produces links like
# "https://app.example.com/reset-password?token=…".
# ⚠️ REQUIRED WHENEVER RESEND_API_KEY IS SET — the process throws at boot if a
#    key is present and this is not, because a reset email carrying a link to
#    nowhere is worse than no email at all.
# 🔴 THE LINK SCHEME IS AN OPEN DECISION — D-WS9-231. The server mints https://,
#    which is what both live options produce; only "keep kiwi://" would change
#    it, and that is one function (buildAppLink) if Hans rules that way.
PUBLIC_APP_URL=""

# ⚪ Where the D-WS9-226 `ai_gapfill` review digest is sent (Hans's address).
# ⚠️ NOT READ BY ANY CODE YET — message 3 is not built. Listed here so the
#    contract is complete and the variable is not rediscovered later.
EMAIL_REVIEW_RECIPIENT=""

# ── Meal images (Row 5 · D-WS9-246 / D-WS9-248) ─────────────────────────
# The image key + bucket are read ONLY by lib/images/live.ts. A missing
# OpenAI key makes generation return { reason: "no_api_key" }: a queued meal
# is deferred (no strike) and keeps rendering the gradient. Nothing here is
# required to boot. (Block 1c: the Pexels / Pixabay stock keys are GONE with
# the stock step — "AI for every image, no exceptions".)

# 🔴 OpenAI key for gpt-image-1-mini. Generations are logged to LLMCallLog
# with mode=image and priced from ai.model_rate.gpt-image-1-mini.* so the
# D-WS9-240 daily ceiling sums them. Org-wide limit 5 images/minute — which
# is why a save only ENQUEUES and the scheduled drain generates.
OPENAI_API_KEY=""

# ⚪ Who may call POST /api/internal/images/drain (the queue's drain, fired by
# Cloud Scheduler once a minute with an OIDC identity token): the job's
# service-account email (comma-separated allowlist) and the token audience
# the job was created with (Cloud Scheduler defaults it to the target URL).
# NOT SECRETS — configuration. Either unset → the route answers 404 to
# everyone and logs image_drain_not_configured (fail closed).
IMAGE_DRAIN_OIDC_EMAIL=""
IMAGE_DRAIN_OIDC_AUDIENCE=""

# ⚪ GCS bucket the resized images are written to and served from
# (https://storage.googleapis.com/<bucket>/meals/<mealId>.jpg). Absent:
# "kiwi-prod-508416-images". Auth is Application Default Credentials — the
# Cloud Run runtime identity in production, `gcloud auth application-default
# login` on a dev box. THERE IS NO KEY FILE AND NO CREDENTIAL PATH VARIABLE.
KIWI_IMAGE_BUCKET="kiwi-prod-508416-images"

# ── Instacart link-out (Row 8) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Neither variable is required to boot. Boot logs ONE line — `instacart:
# configured` or `instacart: not configured (missing …)`, names only — and
# POST /grocery-lists/:id/instacart-link answers 503 retailer_not_configured
# while either is absent. The feature is ALSO behind the SystemSetting
# `retailer.instacart_enabled` (seeded false → 403 retailer_disabled).

# 🔴 Instacart Developer Platform API key. The `keys.` prefix Instacart
# issues is PART of the key — paste it whole. A dev key only works against the
# dev host below; a production key is issued after Instacart's app review.
INSTACART_API_KEY=""

# ⚪ Host of the Instacart Developer Platform, scheme + host, no trailing
# slash, NO DEFAULT (absent means "not configured", never "prod"):
#   dev   https://connect.dev.instacart.tools
#   prod  https://connect.instacart.com
INSTACART_API_BASE_URL=""

# ── Row 13 "Test Kitchen" — the guest funnel ────────────────────────────
# Nothing here is required to boot, and with all of it unset the guest lane
# still works: no bot check, no guest ceiling, no sweep. Set them before the
# funnel is public.
#
# ⚠️ THE PER-IP CAP IS NOT IN THIS FILE BECAUSE IT IS NOT A VARIABLE OF ITS
#    OWN. "3 guest sessions per IP per rolling 24 h" is gated on
#    TRUST_PROXY_HOPS > 0 (top of this file) and is INERT until that is
#    measured — at 0, req.ip is Google's front end for every visitor and the
#    cap would be one global bucket of three sessions a day for everyone.

# ── BUG-313 — the THREE SPEND-GUARD VARS THAT ALREADY EXISTED ────────────
#
# lib/spendGuard.ts has read these since D-WS9-240; Block 1 documented only the
# guest pair below beside them, so the three older levers were live on the
# service and undocumented here — the one file anyone reads to find out what
# knobs a revision has. Semantics copied from that file's header. UNSET = THE
# CHECK IS DISABLED, for all three: nothing here changes behaviour until set.
# A var that is SET but unparseable also disables its own check (a typo must
# not take the app down) and is logged loudly at boot by
# validateSpendGuardEnv() (BUG-263).

# 🔴 The global kill switch. Truthy → EVERY AI call is refused, seeds and CLI
# runs included — it is a deliberate manual act and must mean off. The only one
# of the three that applies to system-triggered (null-userId) callers.
AI_DISABLED=""

# 🔴 The USER daily ceiling in USD. Sums costEstimateUsd for the current UTC day
# over rows WHERE userId IS NOT NULL — so it partitions the ledger against
# AI_GUEST_DAILY_CEILING_USD below, and a system row (both ids null) is in
# neither. Unset = off.
# ⚠️ The proposed 10 was derived from a 9-user sample in which ONE account was
# 59% of all user-attributed rows. RE-DERIVE BEFORE THE USER BASE GROWS: at 50
# users a $10/day ceiling is an outage, not a guard (spendGuard.ts, 2026-09-13).
AI_DAILY_CEILING_USD=""

# 🔴 The per-user daily call cap. COUNT(*) for THIS userId over the current UTC
# day ≥ cap → refuse that user only, nobody else. Unset = off. Measured basis
# for the proposed 500: per-user p95 was 190 calls/day, 84 with a CLI audit day
# excluded.
AI_USER_DAILY_CALLS=""

# 🔴 The GUEST kill switch (D-WS9-261). Truthy → every guest AI call is
# refused; signed-in users are untouched. Hans: "if I'm hitting that and no
# signups, I can kill it before it hurts much." Unset = off.
AI_GUEST_DISABLED=""

# 🔴 The GUEST daily ceiling in USD (D-WS9-261), SEPARATE from
# AI_DAILY_CEILING_USD. Sums costEstimateUsd for the current UTC day over rows
# with guestSessionId IS NOT NULL — the two sums partition the ledger and
# neither sees the other's spend. Unset = off. Ruled 25.
# Measured basis: a catalog-only generation is ONE call
# (wizard.set_preferences.generate) at $0.036 — so $25 is ~690 generations a
# day, not the ~200 the scope doc estimated from a with-live-slots figure.
AI_GUEST_DAILY_CEILING_USD="25"

# ⚪ Cloudflare Turnstile secret (D-WS9-262). Mounted on POST /guest/session
# ONLY. Unset → the route accepts every caller and boot logs one
# `turnstile_disabled` warning. Set → FAIL CLOSED: missing token, rejected
# token, 10 s verify timeout and transport error all answer 403
# bot_check_failed.
# ⚠️ NOT MOUNTED ON SIGNUP, deliberately: the native app cannot solve a web
#    widget, so signup would need a native exemption — and an exemption a
#    client can claim is one an attacker can claim. That stays BUG-222.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=""

# ⚪ The guest sweep's OIDC pair — the exact shape IMAGE_DRAIN_OIDC_* uses.
# Either unset → POST /api/internal/guest/sweep answers 404 to everyone
# (fail closed), so a scheduler pointed at an unconfigured revision shows up
# as a failing job rather than a silent no-op.
GUEST_SWEEP_OIDC_EMAIL=""
GUEST_SWEEP_OIDC_AUDIENCE=""
